menu "VP8 decoder (libvpx_vp8)"
    depends on MUSE_VIDEO_VP8

    choice MUSE_VP8_IRAM
        prompt "VP8 decoder code in IRAM"
        default MUSE_VP8_IRAM_COMPACT if MUSE_VIDEO_DECODER_IRAM
        default MUSE_VP8_IRAM_NONE
        help
            How much of the decoder runs from IRAM (linker.lf): from flash
            it shares the instruction cache with Wi-Fi, BLE and the panel,
            from IRAM it takes internal RAM. Sizes are the ESP32-S31's
            (the ESP-Mosaico video build).

        config MUSE_VP8_IRAM_FULL
            bool "Full: every per-macroblock object, fastest (about 45 KB)"
            help
                The decoder's per-macroblock code with its unrolled filters
                and the low-memory mode's code.

        config MUSE_VP8_IRAM_COMPACT
            bool "Compact: the same objects, smaller code (about 33 KB)"
            help
                The per-macroblock objects without loop unrolling or the
                6-tap filter's per-width copies (VP8_MGX_COMPACT: the same
                arithmetic, bit-exact), and with the low-memory mode's code
                in flash. Within a few KB of stock libvpx's placement.

        config MUSE_VP8_IRAM_HOT
            bool "Hot: tokens, transforms, inter prediction, bilinear (about 12 KB)"
            help
                Most of the decode time for streams with bilinear prediction
                and no loop filter (the phone app's settings); the 6-tap
                filter, loop filter and intra prediction run from flash.

        config MUSE_VP8_IRAM_NONE
            bool "None: everything in flash"
    endchoice

endmenu
